-- blend and the theme in its vertex colour. Tint white as well for the flat look, leave it alone for the metal one. A notint
-- piece is one rectangle called colour, drawn as it is, and a second called value, its brightness alone, for when it is to
-- wear an accent instead of its own colours. A piece with a kind was generated by the build and is one white rectangle
-- called colour that the game colours, added over what is under it for a glow and blended for a fill.
--
-- draw is the height the piece is meant to be drawn at, aspect its width over its height.
--
-- slice says where a piece stretches, as fractions along axis. Two numbers are its two ends and what lies between them
-- stretches. Four are two runs that stretch either side of an ornament that does not, between the middle two. hole is the
-- opening a gem, an icon or a tray's surface shows through, as left, right, top and bottom fractions of the piece, and
-- setting the box of an ornament in the middle of a strip that is drawn filled rather than open, well the dark inside of
-- that ornament within its metal, where a stone is laid over it. body is the top and bottom of the part of a strip its words
-- belong in, as fractions of its height. stones are the boxes of the stones set in a strip's two ends, left then right, each
-- as left, right, top and bottom fractions of the piece. point is how far down a strip the tips of its ends are, as a fraction of its height.
--
-- nine is a frame's corners as left, right, top and bottom fractions, everything between them stretching. edge is how many
-- drawn pixels of rim each side has, from its straight outer line inward, and bleed how far the drawing stands proud of that
-- line. ground is how far in from those lines a window's ground starts, so that none of it shows past a corner, the frame
-- carrying its own surface wherever that leaves a gap inside it. depth is how far a tray drops below the edge it is set in,
-- and a tray's ground runs up to meet the window's.
--

